{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 9, :comments ["<b>When she profanes herself through harlotry.</b> When she is profaned through harlotry — that she had the status of a wife and committed harlotry, whether from betrothal or from marriage. And our Sages disagree on the matter, and all agree that Scripture did not speak of an unmarried girl (see Sanhedrin 51)." "<b>She profanes her father.</b> She profanes and degrades his honor, for they say of him: Cursed be he who fathered this one, cursed be he who raised this one (ibid.)."], :book :leviticus, :voice :rashi, :lang :en, :chapter 21, :notes {}, :source-witnesses nil, :timestamp "2026-08-02T09:07:32.185546853Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}